# Executed-page cache. A committed _freeze entry is what makes a page immune to the CI
# cache key (see docs/_quarto-ci.yml): the results ship with the repo, so a change to
# src/ can never force a re-run. Only pages CI genuinely cannot execute may ship one, so
# deny by default and allow those explicitly — a new page cannot acquire the exemption by
# accident, only by someone adding a line here and saying why.
docs/_freeze/*
!docs/_freeze/site_libs/
# Need the compiled RTSfreerun twin (x1hsts); CI cannot run these at any price.
!docs/_freeze/examples/
docs/_freeze/examples/*
!docs/_freeze/examples/07-rtsfreerun-twin/
!docs/_freeze/examples/10-srm-hsts/
# Runs anywhere, but 569 s against 67 s for the next slowest page.
!docs/_freeze/examples/13-darm-drift-tracking/

# Agent notes. Deny by default, then allow the durable ones — so new agent scratch
# (plans, todos, shell snapshots, throwaway scripts, rendered mockups) can never be
# committed by accident. See CLAUDE.md §"Agent memory and working notes".
.claude/*
!.claude/memory/
!.claude/NOTES.md
!.claude/docs-wow-features.md

.llm/*
!.llm/*.md
!.llm/ps-book/
.llm/ps-book/*
!.llm/ps-book/README.md

# Generated demo figures (local quick-look artifacts; SVG per the graphics rule)
experiments/rtsfreerun/*.png
experiments/rtsfreerun/*.svg
experiments/rtsfreerun/*.npz

# Copyrighted reference textbook — local-only, NEVER publish. This covers both a personal
# PDF copy and any machine-readable scrape of it. `.llm/ps-book/README.md` (a chapter index
# we wrote, no reproduced text) is the only part of the book's shelf that is committed.
docs/SysID-Pintelon.pdf
.llm/ps-book/full-text*

# In-browser Pyodide wheel (built by the docs pre-render hook)
docs/_wheels/
.superpowers/
